<?xml version="1.0"?>
<Container version="2">
  <Name>pia-iptv</Name>
  <Repository>gjergjk/pia-iptv:latest</Repository>
  <Registry>https://hub.docker.com/r/gjergjk/pia-iptv</Registry>
  <Network>bridge</Network>
  <Privileged>false</Privileged>
  <Support>https://github.com/GeorgeAL78/pia-iptv/issues</Support>
  <Project>https://github.com/GeorgeAL78/pia-iptv</Project>
  <Overview>PIA VPN gateway for IPTV, with a kill switch.

Other containers (such as m3u-editor) join this container's network and reach the internet only through Private Internet Access. If the tunnel drops, their traffic is blocked instead of leaking your real IP.

• WireGuard (default) or OpenVPN, any PIA region
• Kill switch: IPv4 locked to the tunnel, IPv6 blocked
• Reconnects in place; re-registers the WireGuard key with server failover
• Only the ports you list are reachable from your LAN

Install this first, then "m3u-editor (via pia-iptv)". The app's ports are published HERE, because it lives in this container's network.</Overview>
  <Category>Network:VPN: MediaServer:Video:</Category>
  <WebUI>http://[IP]:[PORT:36400]/</WebUI>
  <TemplateURL>https://raw.githubusercontent.com/GeorgeAL78/unraid-templates/main/pia-iptv.xml</TemplateURL>
  <Icon>https://raw.githubusercontent.com/GeorgeAL78/pia-qbittorrent-docker/master/readme/icon.png</Icon>
  <ExtraParams>--restart=unless-stopped --cap-add=NET_ADMIN --device=/dev/net/tun --sysctl net.ipv6.conf.all.disable_ipv6=1 --sysctl net.ipv6.conf.default.disable_ipv6=1</ExtraParams>
  <Requires>A Private Internet Access subscription. /dev/net/tun on the server (check with: ls -l /dev/net/tun).</Requires>

